= III/ MATERIALS AND METHODS

== 1/ Materials

Dopamine hydrochloride ($"Dopamine" dot "HCl"$, ≥98% (TLC), powder) was obtained from Sigma-Aldrich. The phosphate buffer solution was prepared using $0.1"M" "KH"_2 "PO"_4$ (≥99.0%, AR grade, Xilong) and $0.1"M" "Na"_2 "HPO"_4 dot 12 "H"_2"O"$ (AR grade, CAS 10039-32-4, Xilong). The acidic CA proton-doping buffer was prepared using $"KCl"$ (≥99.5% AR grade, CAS 7447-40-7, Xilong) and $"HCl"$ (36.0–38.0% AR grade, CAS 7647-01-0, Xilong) for pH adjustment. All aqueous solutions were prepared using deionized water ($3.5"M"Omega dot "cm"$) from a Milli-Q purification system from the Institute of Chemistry, Vietnam Academy of Science and Technology (VAST). Crossbar-patterned and full-surface ITO-coated glass substrates were ultrasonically cleaned in acetone and isopropyl alcohol (AR grade, ≥99.7%, Xilong Chemical) before use.

== 2/ Sample preparation

